  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education: Youth Connect</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The audiences for this programme are:&#x25fc; Young people, potential leaders (15-35) and marginalised groups.&#x25fc; Youth focused organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary benefit of the programme is to ODA countries, as the programmes will take place mostly in those countries.  The change we make:&#x25fc; 1.Young people develop relevant skills and are motivated to apply them.&#x25fc; 2.Create a sustainable ecosystem of education, civil society, cultural and governmental institutions working in coalition to promote cohesion and trust building.&#x25fc; 3.Young people are able to recognise and work positively to reduce gender and other inequalities. &#x25fc; 4.Support the UK&#x2019;s commitments to the Sustainable Development Goals (SDG&#x2019;s).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Connect is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. The primary focus of this Global Programme is ODA eligible activity and outcomes.Youth Connect is our global youth leadership programme which supports young people to develop the skills, inspiration and connections to tackle major challenges, such as climate change, employability and inequality.Youth Connect aims to provide young people with the applicable skills-for-life they need to achieve their own aspirations, follow positive pathways and contribute to more inclusive and positive societies. It creates a stronger environment for positive, values-driven youth action, particularly for women and girls, so that youth-led action contributes to addressing 21st century challenges and achieving the SDG&#x2019;s.</narrative>
  </description>
